                                                "sense_id": "879e5789-19ff-3577-8e42-b259b70d5cda",
                                                "text": "Some of the weeds that cause an undesirable flavor in milk are: onion, tarweed, scaleweed, garlic, mustard, pepper grass."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fe42a5f8-b57a-4877-85f7-e4bbd984a5d8",
                                                "sense_id": "879e5789-19ff-3577-8e42-b259b70d5cda",
                                                "text": "To this group belong feeds such as: Silage, alfalfa hay, turnips, kale, apples, potatoes, beet pulp, beet tops, rape, cabbage; and also weeds such as garlic, scaleweed, dog-fennel, tarweed, peppergrass, wild mustard, and others."
                                            }
